_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n4.5\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.5.stable - macOS Sequoia (15.6.1) - Multi-window, 1 monitor - Metal (Forward+)\n\n### Issue description\n\nIn the GDScript editor, hitting _tab_ usually inserts a visible tab.\nHowever, if the tab comes exactly on a tab stop (ie, at a multiple of four characters), and sits inside a word, then that tab is not displayed.\n\nThis can lead to some really confusing editor messages as GDScript can't parse the hidden whitespace. This can crop up a fair amount if the user's used to tab completion and hits tab too soon, and in the wrong spot.\n\n\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nOpen a new GDScript script.\n\nType this:\n```\nvar hello = \"world\"\n```\nPut the cursor before the `o`. Hit tab. The break is essentially invisible: if you're looking for it, the `o` moves by a pixel or two.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nn/a","closed_by":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received